    "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes #64204. AOT compile cache never loads for Qwen3-Next / Qwen3.5 because the fused QK-norm/RoPE/gate Triton kernel is launched directly inside the compiled graph. This registers it as a vLLM custom op. Also fixes the UTF-8 encoding issue in `_compute_code_hash` noted in the same issue.\n\nNo existing open PR addresses this (searched for `id_to_kernel` and `fused_qk_rmsnorm_rope_gate`; related PRs touch overflow/M-RoPE/ROCm, not cache loading).\n\n## Claims\n\n- Warm starts of Qwen3-Next / Qwen3.5 load the AOT-compiled artifact instead of failing with `Kernel index 1 not found in id_to_kernel` and recompiling (~29s per start in the report).\n- Compile-cache code hashing no longer fails on non-ASCII source files on Windows.\n\n## Validation\n\n- New CPU test `test_fused_qk_norm_rope_gate_traces_as_custom_op`: fails on `main` (tracing enters the raw Triton launch), passes with this PR.",
